{{also|bedridden|bed-ridden}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[bed-ridden]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|bedreda||lang=ang}}, from {{term|rida||lang=ang|rider}}, with {{term|-en}} by analogy with past participle adjectives

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈbɛdɹɪdən/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[confine]]d to [[bed]] because of [[infirmity]] or [[illness]]
#* Macaulay
#*: The estate of a '''bedridden''' old gentleman.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|confined to bed}} [[bedfast]], [[bedbound]]

